mp":1785849586930075001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"A6-0d oracle card (strong-tier, pre-code). Authoritative contract: current signed ticket plan plus Git bundle/ref semantics exercised through stock Git. Existing coverage inventory: A6-0c covers shared Git subprocess and partial-clone refusal, but repository search found no bundle-create/verify/restore or reclaim-backup tests. Preconditions: clean full unfiltered clone; origin exposes tickets plus ancestor/descendant/diverged/unrelated heads, annotated tag, lightweight blob tag; old tip equals initial remote tickets OID; output paths are absent and outside registered worktrees/Git dirs. Production path: CLI -> exact ls-remote snapshot/de-peel -> local object/type and ancestry classification -> explicit temporary refs -> bundle create/verify -> JSON manifest -> restore probe -> exact remote snapshot comparison -> owned cleanup. Tier: real temporary Git remotes/worktrees/subprocesses; a unit tier cannot prove ref reachability, bundle headers, restore, or no remote mutation. Exact postconditions: manifest inventory/relationships exact, bundle named OID map exact, restore map exact, remote bytes unchanged, no push/delete, outputs atomic/no-overwrite. Recovery: injected bundle-verify failure removes owned outputs/refs and same-clone retry succeeds; simulated abnormal state is refused and a fresh-clone retry succeeds. Contention: exempt from rebar shared-store suites because the helper owns one offline fresh clone and never mutates the ticket store; no cross-clone shared state exists. Surface census: CLI in scope via real subprocess; library facade and MCP/API out of scope for one-time ops; A6-1 automated caller is deferred but consumes the same CLI; dual direction in scope through create+restore. Gate: exact integration node, then make lint/typecheck/test. Implementer tier: standard/mid because Git graph classification, atomic artifacts, and recovery span one production file and one integration harness; only the happy path will remain visible.","timestamp":1785849675350236001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"A6-0d real rehearsal receipt (fresh full unfiltered clone; non-shallow; helper invocation performed no push/delete and its exact heads/tags snapshot was unchanged through completion). First attempt failed closed before artifacts because origin/tickets advanced after clone; refreshed exclusively owned clone then succeeded with BACKUP READY. Bundle: /tmp/rebar-a6-0d-rehearsal.0OC5dV/artifacts/tickets-before-reclaim.bundle; SHA-256 6fb181f53cb712527bdb6430aa7412b6fb7e963f7f19fcf728f9cca2866185bd; 2029154453 bytes. Manifest: /tmp/rebar-a6-0d-rehearsal.0OC5dV/artifacts/tickets-before-reclaim.json; SHA-256 0ca5cdb99c0f9137a337e91c796d7f6f54d0ee7bfdf6a9ea600ff6ddc4798c50; 7202 bytes. Observed old tickets tip: 2119556b69ebdf039d70fabe40f14d9d2792e8a5. Included pins: remote pre-heal-a118-20260710T005736Z -> 2a77dd48275efffd88ae4b5ab05fc906517b1725; clone-local pre-a3-remediation -> 0adbd40a0a9348ad898db64bae98e4c5556a6de7. Stock git bundle verify: bundle is okay; 3 named refs; complete history; SHA-1. Manifest enumerated 35 canonical remote heads/tags. Post-run clone had no refs/reclaim-backup/ refs and clean status. A6-0d helper changed no remote ref. This receipt comment and later store writes advance tickets normally: A6-1 MUST create a fresh final bundle after quiescence whenever its observed quiet-window old tip differs from 2119556b69ebdf039d70fabe40f14d9d2792e8a5.","timestamp":1785850737010692001}],"created_at":1785372528519202001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"761fba27-9623-40b5-b48a-11a09cd10589","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"6d50-8449-e71a-45b4"},{"link_uuid":"e82e1a1a-071a-4ba3-94b4-6dc2d963235d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b634-d8db-cdb8-4416"},{"link_uuid":"63a4e7fb-4d2d-45d4-bbcf-b646d08622d2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2c05-c21c-91d0-421c"}],"description":"Prepare the committed helper and a verified real rehearsal artifact needed by the reclaim window. This story performs no remote ref deletion and never pushes. A6-1 alone refreshes the bundle if `origin/tickets` moved, deletes identified pins, and publishes the rewrite after all writers are quiesced. Session log 1cb6-d553-6565-49b4 contains measured facts.\n\n## Context\n\nRemote tag `refs/tags/pre-heal-a118-20260710T005736Z` and host-local tag `refs/tags/pre-a3-remediation` retain pre-rewrite history. An in-repository backup ref would defeat reclamation, so rollback material must be a bundle outside every Git worktree and Git directory. Live ref OIDs are derived at execution time rather than from measured counts or hardcoded IDs.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Add `infra/scripts/prepare_reclaim_backup.py`, a stock-Git CLI for a clean, unfiltered clone owned exclusively by one invocation. It accepts the old tickets tip, an off-repo bundle path, a JSON manifest path, and repeatable pin-ref names. Import A6-0c `run_git`, `ref_name`, `is_partial_clone`, and `ReclaimError` from `reclaim_bridge_history.py` so safety behavior cannot drift.\n- Enumerate `git ls-remote --heads --tags origin` at run time, collapse annotated-tag `^{}` lines onto canonical refs, and record every head/tag with exact direct and peeled OIDs. For each commit tip, record one relationship to the old tip: same, old-tip-is-ancestor, ref-is-ancestor, diverged-with-merge-base, unrelated, or non-commit.\n- Refuse a clone containing any pre-existing `refs/reclaim-backup/` ref and name the fresh-clone remedy. Create one run-unique namespace beneath that prefix. Normal success and caught failures remove only that invocation namespace in `finally`; abnormal termination recovery is to discard the clone and rerun in a fresh unfiltered clone. Separate concurrent clones share no local refs, cannot overwrite existing artifact paths, and perform no remote write.\n- Resolve requested pins from live enumeration or the local clone and refuse missing/non-commit pins. Build the bundle from explicit temporary refs for the old tip and pins, then verify it.\n- Refuse partial/promisor clones. Refuse bundle or manifest paths inside the repository, its Git directory, or another registered worktree. Create parent directories only outside those boundaries and never overwrite an artifact.\n- Restore the bundle into a throwaway repository and compare the restored old-tip and pin-tip OIDs exactly. Snapshot origin heads/tags before and after; no push, delete, or remote mutation is permitted.\n- Run against a fresh real unfiltered clone and store the rehearsal bundle/manifest outside the repository. Record paths, SHA-256 checksums, sizes, old tip, pin tips, and bundle verification. A6-1 creates a fresh final bundle after quiescence whenever its old tip differs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] The helper enumerates every live origin head/tag at run time without a hardcoded count. Tier: temporary real Git remotes.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] The manifest collapses annotated-tag `^{}` lines while retaining exact direct and peeled OIDs. Tier: temporary real Git remotes.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Every enumerated commit ref receives exactly one old-tip relationship. Tier: real Git fixtures for same, ancestor, descendant, diverged, and unrelated histories.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A non-commit ref is recorded without an ancestry command on that object. Tier: real Git remote with a blob ref.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Partial/promisor clone refusal exits nonzero before creating refs or artifacts and names a fresh-unfiltered-clone remedy. Tier: CLI integration.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Any output destination inside a registered worktree or Git directory is refused. Tier: real worktree integration parameterized for bundle and manifest.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Any pre-existing output artifact is not overwritten. Tier: CLI integration parameterized for bundle and manifest.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] The bundle named-ref map exactly matches the expected old-tip plus requested pin-tip OIDs. Tier: real Git bundle integration.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] `git bundle verify` succeeds for the completed bundle. Tier: real Git bundle integration.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Bundle restore reproduces the full expected old-tip plus pin-tip OID map. Tier: real Git restore integration.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A recording Git wrapper observes no push or remote-delete invocation. Tier: CLI integration.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Origin heads/tags output is byte-identical before and after success. Tier: real Git comparison.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A caught verification failure leaves no incomplete artifact or current-run helper ref. Tier: fault-injected real-repository integration.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A pre-existing helper ref causes a nonzero fresh-clone-remedy result without deleting that ref. Tier: real Git ref integration.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Retrying from a fresh clone after simulated abnormal termination succeeds with current requested OIDs. Tier: killed-process integration.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] A ticket comment records both rehearsal artifact absolute paths.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] A ticket comment records SHA-256 checksums and byte sizes for both artifacts.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] A ticket comment records the observed old tip and included pin tips.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] A ticket comment records successful `git bundle verify` output.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] A ticket comment confirms A6-0d changed no remote ref.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] A ticket comment requires A6-1 to recreate the final bundle when its quiet-window old tip differs.\n\n## Verification commands\n\n- `pytest tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py -v`\n- `make lint`\n- `make typecheck`\n- `make test`\n\n## Scope\n\n`infra/scripts/prepare_reclaim_backup.py` and `tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py`. No source-module, configuration, or remote-ref mutation. Scope: M. Depends on closed A6-0c; A6-1 consumes the helper and owns final refresh/deletion/publication.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/prepare_reclaim_backup.py","reason":"stock-Git ref manifest and off-repo bundle preparation helper"},{"path":"tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py","reason":"real-repository enumeration, bundle, restore, safety, and recovery oracle"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","6d50-8449-e71a-45b4"],["parent","0303-692c-55dc-4a18"],["relates_to","2c05-c21c-91d0-421c"],["relates_to","b634-d8db-cdb8-4416"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0303-692c-55dc-4a18","parent_status_uuid":"9dda5997-2605-4764-98a1-432fcf95960c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ae8a-5244-99c3-4e1d","ticket_type":"story","title":"A6-0d: prepare ref-hygiene manifest and off-repo backup bundle","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["82946cbe-89fd-4e8d-a67f-7f9f00d862d8","f4c4263d-bc1f-4c71-88f3-671410247224","26dae0be-9e3e-4939-9ae5-bb9d46883612","761fba27-9623-40b5-b48a-11a09cd10589","68d07b47-7af4-4442-94e3-3b781da6fd1d","859e1d63-d7bd-442e-b6ae-c68c6a5d364b","c80a5ddb-cd88-4fef-874c-6574b4664b62","ead8364a-7b97-4295-8d72-6f7654d6bec0","a99e1fc9-17b3-45b6-968c-f09bb489968c","1d5d863f-3b40-4686-9fbb-b5e666c4fc7f","9aab1f62-83b2-46aa-aaf8-06f2300f1d95","a76ee15a-7172-4568-aef5-4224193007b7","9ab452f3-3d49-4ac8-94b8-b22fc6c19630","f117827f-87cc-4fd3-9b80-7215348d5538","9dda5997-2605-4764-98a1-432fcf95960c","fc26062f-67c4-4f10-860a-05c50128efaf","069e1ccb-7dfc-418f-9b32-71aff565d92c","a9ac543d-621e-4ac8-bfaa-a584cbe17fec","e82e1a1a-071a-4ba3-94b4-6dc2d963235d","63a4e7fb-4d2d-45d4-bbcf-b646d08622d2"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785853444647660002,"uuid":"c3a6cb79-4a7b-41da-9cae-e32dd05cb71d"}